      "evidence": "The interviewer repeatedly used the exact phrase 'Before we move on, could you answer the question above?' throughout the intake, which felt mechanical and unnecessary."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "inefficient_questioning",
      "evidence": "In the PHQ-9 and GAD-7 sections, the interviewer frequently had to re-state the entire list of options because the patient was confused, which is understandable, but the interviewer's reliance on the full script rather than simplifying the prompt contributed to the patient's repeated confusion."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "redundant_questioning",
      "evidence": "The interviewer asked 'Are there any further medical conditions you’ve been diagnosed with?' and then immediately followed up with 'I mean any other diagnosed medical conditions besides high cholesterol. Are there any others?' after the patient had already indicated they were unsure."
